# Google Identity Services (Sign in with Google).
#
# The OAuth client id is a PUBLIC identifier — Google puts it in the page —
# but it is still per-deployment build config, so it is not committed. Copy
# this file to `.env.local` and fill it in, or set the variable in the
# deployment environment.
#
# Get one at https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials → "Create
# credentials" → "OAuth client ID" → "Web application", and add your origin
# (e.g. http://localhost:5173) to "Authorised JavaScript origins".
#
# Leave it unset and the app degrades to an explicit, clearly-labelled
# "Continue as a demo user" path — no Google script is loaded at all.
#
# There is no client SECRET here and there must never be one: the GIS web
# flow returns an ID token to the browser and uses no secret. Anything that
# needs verifying is verified server-side against Google's JWKS.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
